<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean 3-yr yields end up on bearish buying.</title>
<headline>S.Korean 3-yr yields end up on bearish buying.</headline>
<text>
<p>Yields on three-year benchmark corporate bonds closed higher on Tuesday as most investors stayed disinterested amid uncertain market prospects, brokers said.</p>
<p>But three-month certificates of deposits dropped as institutions increased purchases of short-term instruments.</p>
<p>* 3-yr corporates close at 12.25 vs 12.10</p>
<p>* 3-mth CDs end at 12.15 vs 12.20</p>
<p>* Overnight average call rates unchanged at 11.4 -------------------------------------------------------</p>
</text>
